	quests: [
		{
			description: [
				"Welcome dear reader. If you find yourself perusing these pages, I assume you must seek the secrets of the most pure of sciences, &e&lAlchemy&r, am I incorrect? Well you are in luck, for I will guide you through the process of learning the ins and outs of this magnificent practice."
				"And, prithee, pay no mind to those foolish chemists and physicists trying to dissuade you from your noble pursuit: Alchemy isn't a made-up fable, but rather a magnificent art that will elevate you onto greater heights! So follow my words, and become a true folk of science with me."
			]
			icon: {
				Count: 1
				id: "modonomicon:modonomicon"
				tag: {
					"modonomicon:book_id": "theurgy:the_hermetica"
					"modonomicon:book_open_state": "closed"
				}
			}
			id: "485D79874FC63DF0"
			rewards: [{
				id: "3876EF0E59C3A4D5"
				item: {
					Count: 1
					id: "modonomicon:modonomicon"
					tag: {
						"modonomicon:book_id": "theurgy:the_hermetica"
						"modonomicon:book_open_state": "closed"
					}
				}
				type: "item"
			}]
			size: 2.0d
			subtitle: "Their foolish ignorance..."
			tasks: [{
				id: "4B5A1624DCA56984"
				title: "Take the mantle of alchemist"
				type: "checkmark"
			}]
			title: "The rejected science"
			x: 0.0d
			y: 0.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["485D79874FC63DF0"]
			description: [
				"The book I gave you, while in itself worthy of proper study, seems to carry some information that does not correlate with reality. The scholars who produced that book were certainly well read and wise, but they clearly ail from far, far away, where things are much different than here. Fear not my pupil, for I have all the answers you need to become the best you can be."
				"{@pagebreak}"
				"Now, onto our first alchemical venture. The most important component of all is &dSal Ammoniac&r, a solvent present in many alchemical reactions. It seems to be unusually scarce in these lands, mining for it won't yield any result, but fear not! The waters contain traces of this substance within themselves, and it's possible to extract them through evaporation."
				"{@pagebreak}"
				"This is where our first apparati come in. First of all is the &5Sal Ammoniac Accumulator&r, which will be our vessel from which to extract the precious solvent. Now you'll need a &dSal Ammoniac Tank&r placed below the accumulator. When water is poured into the accumulator, liquid sal ammoniac will deposit into the tank below for later use."
				"{image:kubejs:textures/quests/sal_ammoniac.png width:160 height:75 align:center}"
			]
			hide_until_deps_complete: true
			icon: "theurgy:sal_ammoniac_accumulator"
			id: "771EB24CF9C3BFC7"
			rewards: [{
				count: 5
				id: "77FFE8309A77F298"
				item: "theurgy:sal_ammoniac_crystal"
				type: "item"
			}]
			subtitle: "And some elucidation..."
			tasks: [
				{
					id: "4E4A7CF9A7E094B7"
					item: "theurgy:sal_ammoniac_accumulator"
					type: "item"
				}
				{
					id: "61BCB884C8579936"
					item: "theurgy:sal_ammoniac_tank"
					type: "item"
				}
			]
			title: "The first venture"
			x: 2.3d
			y: 0.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["771EB24CF9C3BFC7"]
			description: ["As I have previously stated, these lands have unusually scarce amounts of the precious solvent, but occasionally one may find large deposits of a mineral called &9Zircon&r. While useless to most, this mineral actually holds the key to source greater amounts of sal ammoniac than through evaporation. While better methods of extracting it will come through alchemy, for the time being simply blasting crushed zircon will coerce some of the solvent to crystallize."]
			icon: "theurgy:sal_ammoniac_crystal"
			id: "03FE8AE33604E86B"
			rewards: [{
				count: 5
				id: "4BDACEE09BE3FF34"
				item: "immersivegeology:crushed_ore_zircon"
				type: "item"
			}]
			subtitle: "These lands are deceiving"
			tasks: [{
				id: "4356F86ED3371C6F"
				title: "Where to find more Sal Ammoniac?"
				type: "checkmark"
			}]
			x: 2.3d
			y: 1.4d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["771EB24CF9C3BFC7"]
			description: [
				"The stage is set my dear pupil, it's now time to begin your first real application of alchemy. I will explain to you the art of liquefaction, from which to extract an element's sulfur."
				"{@pagebreak}"
				"First you'll need a &cPyromantic Brazier&r, an apparatus that, when fueled, will provide heat for the reaction. Above the brazier you will need a &6Liquefaction Cauldron&r, with which you will be conducting the extraction."
				"By placing an element and some liquid sal ammoniac in the cauldron as well as lighting up the brazier below it, the element will be reduced to its sulfur."
				"{image:kubejs:textures/quests/liquefaction.png width:160 height:75 align:center}"
				"{@pagebreak}"
				"&6Alchemical Sulfur&r can be interpreted as the soul or identity of an element, and it determines what element will be synthesized by the process of incubation, which we will go over later on."
				"{@pagebreak}"
				"The Hermetica speaks of metal triplication within its pages. Now, the scholarly authors of this book clearly had different raw materials at hand that allowed this practice to be true all the time, but where you and I are from, this is not completely true. Different ores can be liquefied into relevant sulfurs, but only rich ore clumps will yield the triplified sulfur spoken of in the text."
				"Alchemy does however remain a valid way to easily extract useful minerals from the unrefined ore, even without an increase in gain."
			]
			hide_until_deps_complete: true
			icon: "theurgy:liquefaction_cauldron"
			id: "1B1FCB43DA063F22"
			rewards: [{
				count: 5
				id: "6CFA0D5004B75550"
				item: "theurgy:sal_ammoniac_crystal"
				type: "item"
			}]
			subtitle: "Extracting the soul"
			tasks: [
				{
					id: "003C8DD2D912FE14"
					item: "theurgy:liquefaction_cauldron"
					type: "item"
				}
				{
					id: "4BD6C512AC99EE2B"
					item: "theurgy:pyromantic_brazier"
					type: "item"
				}
			]
			title: "Alchemical Liquefaction"
			x: 4.3d
			y: 0.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: [
				"1B1FCB43DA063F22"
				"6F60F3E872AC8886"
				"08C47EC5D4D10B8E"
			]
			description: [
				"Now that all three base components have been aquired, it's time to put them back together. To this end, you will require an &eIncubator&r, an apparatus capable of reforming matter from base components. The machine will require three different vessels, one for each base component, to be placed at its sides, as well as a heat source."
				"{@pagebreak}"
				"Once the structure is built, you may proceed by inserting the relevant ingredients in the appropriate vessels, then by providing heat to the machine. If the operation is running, the incubator will release smoke from its top, and once it stops the desired element will be present inside the apparatus."
				"{image:kubejs:textures/quests/incubator.png width:160 height:75 align:center}"
			]
			hide_until_deps_complete: true
			icon: "theurgy:incubator"
			id: "56DD5940D614ED82"
			shape: "octagon"
			subtitle: "Rebuilding the element"
			tasks: [{
				id: "37BCA407CF7950C4"
				item: "theurgy:incubator"
				type: "item"
			}]
			title: "Alchemical Incubation"
			x: 5.6d
			y: 0.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["771EB24CF9C3BFC7"]
			description: [
				"The stage is set my dear pupil, it's now time to begin your first real application of alchemy. I will explain to you the art of calcination, from which to extract an element's salt."
				"{@pagebreak}"
				"First you'll need a &cPyromantic Brazier&r, an apparatus that, when fueled, will provide heat for the reaction. Above the brazier you will need a &7Calcination Oven&r, with which you will be conducting the extraction."
				"When an element is placed in the oven, it will be reduced down to its most essential physical component, its salt."
				"{image:kubejs:textures/quests/calcination.png width:160 height:75 align:center}"
				"{@pagebreak}"
				"&7Alchemical Salt&r can be interpreted as the body of an element, and it gives elements a physical component to be synthesized into by the process of incubation, which we will go over later on."
			]
			hide_dependency_lines: true
			hide_until_deps_complete: true
			icon: "theurgy:calcination_oven"
