		}
		{
			dependencies: ["56DD5940D614ED82"]
			description: [
				"As I have previously stated, mercury is the energy contained within matter. This force is not only used in incubation processes, but it can be exploited for other uses as well. It all begins with a &9Mercury Catalyst&r, an apparatus capableof breaking down mercury into its flux form. Mercury flux is a freeform version of mercury, essentially the closest thing we have to pure energy that can still be manipulated."
				"{@pagebreak}"
				"Once the catalyst breaks down solid mercury into flux, it can be used by specific apparati. One such device is the &cCaloric Flux Emitter&r, which will provide heat to any apparatus that needs it, removing the need for pyromantic braziers. Simply linking the flux emitter to an apparatus and placing it to a nearby catalyst will allow it to work. By default, the emitters will constantly drain flux to do their work, but by providing them with a redstone signal they can be stopped."
				"{image:kubejs:textures/quests/caloric_flux.png width:160 height:75 align:center}"
			]
			hide_until_deps_complete: true
			icon: "theurgy:mercury_catalyst"
			id: "38A91E6356A41DDB"
			rewards: [{
				count: 2
				id: "30C5C04E97FC8AA3"
				item: "theurgy:caloric_flux_emitter"
				type: "item"
			}]
			subtitle: "The gateway to true material mastery"
			tasks: [
				{
					id: "6E21F8F2C7A5C9B1"
					item: "theurgy:mercury_catalyst"
					type: "item"
				}
				{
					id: "55E7F58F3E6AB080"
					item: "theurgy:caloric_flux_emitter"
					type: "item"
				}
			]
			title: "A refined source of power"
			x: 5.6d
			y: 1.4d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["38A91E6356A41DDB"]
			description: [
				"It's time for you to understand the last alchemical component you will be working with: &3Niters&r. Niters are similar in nature to sulfurs, but unlike those they don't embody a specific element, but rather a wide concept. So a sulfur could embody something like &ocopper&r or &oemerald&r, while a niter would embody something like &ometal&r or &ogem&r. They also come in different tiers depending on the value of the element they were extracted from. So a niter extracted from iron and one extracted from gold would both be the same category of &ometal&r, but the former would be &ocommon&r, while the latter would be &orare&r."
				"{@pagebreak}"
				"Niters are essential because unlike sulfurs, they can be altered into different forms, allowing you to turn one element into another. This process is called &5Replication&r, and can be done in one of three different ways, which we will go over in the following pages."
			]
			icon: "theurgy:alchemical_sulfur_earthen_matters_abundant"
			id: "5E2755FCA8618792"
			subtitle: "Exploring wider concepts"
			tasks: [{
				id: "1B2DC0DA5C69CBFA"
				title: "Understanding Niters"
				type: "checkmark"
			}]
			title: "Understanding Niters"
			x: 9.4d
			y: 1.4d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["5E2755FCA8618792"]
			description: [
				"The first kind of replication is &aReformation&r, a process that allows one type of sulfur to be transformed into another, provided they are of the same type and tier."
				"{@pagebreak}"
				"First you will need a more complex set of apparati. One &cTarget Pedestal&r, up to eight &8Source Pedestals&r, and finally a &eResult Pedestal&r, all linked by a &dSulfuric Flux Emitter&r, which itself necessitates a source of flux. Once these apparati are set, reformation can begin."
				"{image:kubejs:textures/quests/reformation.png width:160 height:75 align:center}"
				"{@pagebreak}"
				"To actually reform sulfur, you will need just two ingredients: the sulfur you wish to replicate, the &oTarget&r, and a sulfur you wish to turn into the target, the &oSource&r. Simply place the sulfurs in their relevant pedestals and you may begin reformation."
			]
			hide_until_deps_complete: true
			icon: "theurgy:reformation_result_pedestal"
			id: "232D6B544D7A8AAC"
			rewards: [{
				count: 16
				id: "55BFA7209EEBF347"
				item: "theurgy:sal_ammoniac_crystal"
				type: "item"
			}]
			subtitle: "Elements of the same type and tier"
			tasks: [
				{
					id: "2A4CA690F15C97C8"
					item: "theurgy:reformation_result_pedestal"
					type: "item"
				}
				{
					id: "1B72253D5446A57C"
					item: "theurgy:reformation_target_pedestal"
					type: "item"
				}
				{
					id: "00852348032F4AE9"
					item: { Count: 2, id: "theurgy:reformation_source_pedestal" }
					type: "item"
				}
				{
					id: "1C9B04E36A0B4462"
					item: "theurgy:sulfuric_flux_emitter"
					type: "item"
				}
			]
			title: "Replication through Reformation"
			x: 11.6d
			y: 1.4d
		}
		{
			dependencies: [
				"5E2755FCA8618792"
				"232D6B544D7A8AAC"
			]
			description: [
				"Now we get into the art of &1Transmutation&r, which allows one to turn a sulfur into another of a different type, provided they're of the same tier. This process will involve your first use of niters."
				"{@pagebreak}"
				"As for how one gets their hands on niter, it's not too difficult. First you will need a &eFermentation Vat&r, then you will require some water, a sulfur and a catalyst. The catalyst can be some type of crop or sapling or even sugar, though a better fermentation starter can be achieved through alchemy. Once all three components have been added to the vat, it's a matter of simply closing the lid and letting it operate undisturbed for a short time, after which the niter will be ready for extraction."
				"{@pagebreak}"
				"Much like with the sulfur before, you will need both a target and a source niter, both of the same tier. Then you will be able to use the reformation apparatus as you would with sulfurs."
				"With this niter you may now reform it a second time, but instead of turning it into another niter you may turn it into a sulfur."
			]
			hide_until_deps_visible: true
			icon: "theurgy:fermentation_vat"
			id: "7B89A3307EA9CFF8"
			rewards: [{
				count: 10
				id: "6062BDA2C958843D"
				item: "theurgy:fermentation_starter"
				type: "item"
			}]
			subtitle: "Elements of the same tier but of different type"
			tasks: [{
				id: "66BDBE0D18F88E1D"
				item: "theurgy:fermentation_vat"
				type: "item"
			}]
			title: "Replication through Transmutation"
			x: 11.6d
			y: 0.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: [
				"5E2755FCA8618792"
				"7B89A3307EA9CFF8"
			]
			description: [
				"At last is the process of &6Exaltation&r,  which allows one to turn a sulfur into another of a different tier, provided they're of the same type."
				"{@pagebreak}"
				"To begin exaltation it's necessary to create one final apparatus, the &3Digestion Vat&r. This machine will require the niter you wish to exalt, some liquid sal ammoniac, and alchemically pure gold, should the desired exaltation be a tier upgrade. Once all the ingredients are provided, the vat will begin exaltation of the provided niter."
				"Once exaltation is complete, you may do with your niter as you wish."
				"{@pagebreak}"
				"Now, as to how you obtain alchemically pure gold, it's not hard at all. You will require an ingot of gold, any alchemical salt, and a whole bucket's worth of water, then you may insert these components into a digestion vat. The salts will incorporate all the impurities into themselves, leaving the gold perfectly pure."
			]
			hide_until_deps_visible: true
			icon: "theurgy:digestion_vat"
			id: "26C3C9BF897A0CCF"
			rewards: [{
				count: 12
				id: "1A2F8C56A7EEAA70"
				item: "theurgy:purified_gold"
				type: "item"
			}]
			subtitle: "Elements of the same type but of different tier"
			tasks: [
				{
					id: "3CAC87AA09C390D7"
					item: "theurgy:digestion_vat"
					type: "item"
				}
				{
					id: "01A6195497478B91"
